" ~/.tridactylrc  --  managed by chezmoi
"
" Ported from qutebrowser quickmarks. All jump targets are `searchurls`
" rather than Tridactyl `quickmark`s: quickmarks are limited to a single
" character (go<key>), whereas searchurls keep semantic multi-word names.
"
" Usage:  o <name>   current tab
"         t <name>   new tab
"         w <name>   new window
"
" None of these URLs contain a %s placeholder, so a bare `o <name>` appends
" nothing and navigates to the URL exactly as written.

" ------------------------------------------------------- tabs / new tab
" New tab page. Tridactyl overrides about:newtab via chrome_url_overrides,
" and `newtab` redirects that override to a URL of your choosing.
" about:blank gives an instant, empty new tab; Tridactyl's binds still work
" because Tridactyl special-cases about:blank (its content script declares
" match_about_blank, and a tab opened from an existing one inherits a
" principal, so the script is injected).
"
" NOTE this does NOT apply to new *windows* -- see the README. A new window's
" first tab is loaded by Firefox from browser.startup.homepage before any
" extension can claim it, and no Tridactyl setting reaches it.
set newtab about:blank

" Tab placement. Tabs are a flat vertical list (Firefox native vertical
" tabs), so "next" is the intuitive behaviour: a tab you open lands directly
" below the one you opened it from rather than at the bottom of a long list.
set tabopenpos next
set relatedopenpos related

